E1 non-vacuous:
  M1 the verdict is decided by the frame beside the emission -> E1 an emission of false is unstable whatever the frame beside it
E2 non-vacuous:
  M3 the absence the record named is dropped from the answer’s list -> E2 a page with no reachable ApplicationRef carries the one absence once, with no zero standing in for it
E3 non-vacuous:
  M4 a settle time is fabricated from the attach reading -> E3 a record that never settled answers no time field and no duration
  M5 a page already stable at attach is presented as a transition after it -> E3 the settle time is the record’s own reading
E5 non-vacuous:
  M6 every recorded entry is counted as a pass of its own -> E5 two TemplateUpdate start/end pairs in one row are two passes over that component
  M7 the passes are counted from the frame’s checks rows, not its events -> E5 two ChangeDetection pairs are two passes attributed to no component
E6 non-vacuous:
  M8 a frame with no paired work is given a pass it did not record -> E6 a frame that recorded no paired work reports no pass at all
  M9 an end with no start of its own pair is counted as a pass -> E6 an end with no start in the frame is no pass
E7 non-vacuous:
  M10 a cause is filled in from the component name the frame recorded -> E7 the answer carries exactly the contract fields and no cause
  M11 an absence the read did not force is rendered as another absence’s sentence -> E7 no-stability-observable renders in its own cell under its own name
E8 non-vacuous:
  M12 an owner is filled in from the component name the frame recorded -> E8 the answer carries no cause, no owner, no call site and no task id
  M13 an opted-in creation stack is carried as an outstanding inventory -> E8 the opted-in fields fill no absence and add none
E10 non-vacuous:
  M14 instability is inferred from a record that emitted nothing -> E10 a record that recorded nothing is not unstable
  M15 the verdict is read out of the frame’s silence rather than the emission -> E10 silence never turns cannot-tell into stable
