  M4 an edge-named effect says the graph labelled it -> E2 namedBy reads recorded-edge (the whole recorded edge)
E3 non-vacuous:
  M5 an empty read borrows a named signal from elsewhere in the graph -> E3 the read is empty rather than borrowed (the counter read with its consumer edges removed, beside a named signal)
  M6 an empty read is reported as an absence instead of a finding -> E3 an effect with no named read is a finding, never an absence (the /stale-view effect, whose graph records no edge at all)
E4 non-vacuous:
  M7 the phase carries a phase word of its own -> E4 the phase carries nothing else (a labelled effect)
  M8 the effect finding carries a phase of its own -> E4 no finding carries a phase (a labelled effect)
  M9 the named absence becomes a phase word -> E4 the phase is cannot-tell with the named absence (a labelled effect)
E5 non-vacuous:
  M10 the message is folded into the effect finding -> E5 the effect and the recorded message stay two findings
  M11 the message is dropped, leaving the effect finding alone -> E5 the effect and the recorded message stay two findings
E6 non-vacuous:
  M12 the message finding names a cause -> E6 the finding names no cause
  M13 the message finding names an effect it was not given -> E6 the finding names no effect
E1 non-vacuous:
  M14 the effectless graph is no longer refused as missing its effect node -> E1 the absence names the missing node the graph lacks (the counter graph with its effect node removed)
  M15 the reason becomes a claim about the page instead of about the node -> E1 the answer never says the page has no effects: {"findings":[{"state":"cannot-tell","reason":"the page has no effects"}],"phase":{"state":"cannot-tell","absence":"no-effect-event"}}
E1 unreadable non-vacuous:
  M16 a fact naming no graph is reported as a graph with no effect node -> E1 an unread graph is never reported as an empty one (no fact at all)
E2 subject non-vacuous:
  M17 a label two effects carry is resolved by taking the first -> E2 the graph does not hold that subject (a label two effects carry)
E8 non-vacuous:
  M18 the reads are sorted instead of kept in the recorded edge order -> E8 the order of reads is the recorded edge order, never a sorted one
  M19 the effect finding carries a value that changes on every read -> E8 the same graph read twice is byte-identical text
